  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>(A) Aldehydes give red precipitate with Fehling&#39;s solution.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0043_ab578a755dc2.png\" style=\"width: 818px; height: 132px;\" /></p><p>(B) Phenols give violet colour with neutral ferric chloride solution</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0043_4bf50f3adb5d.png\" style=\"width: 623px; height: 187px;\" /></p><p>(C) Primary amines give isocyanides with chloroform in the presence of alkali. This reaction known as carbylamine reaction.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0043_692ea7a8e1bb.png\" style=\"width: 396px; height: 162px;\" /></p><p>(D)&nbsp;1-phenylethanol give haloform reaction with sodium hypochlorite. The products are benzoate and chloroform.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0043_78515445c9ee.png\" style=\"width: 550px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>"
